<title>USA: NYCE cotton called to open steady to 0.10 cent up.</title>
<headline>NYCE cotton called to open steady to 0.10 cent up.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>NYCE cotton futures were called to open unchanged to 0.10 cent higher as of 1018 EDT, floor sources said.</p>
<p>They termed neutral the Sparks estimate issued Tuesday. The Memphis-based analytical firm estimated 1997/98 U.S. cotton production at 17.642 million bales, according to trade sources.</p>
<p>USDA in July projected the 1997/98 (Aug 1-July 31) crop at 18 million bales.</p>
<p>((Doris Frankel, Chicago Commodity Desk, 312-983-7305))</p>
